                        "great rapidity",
                        "surprising rapidity"
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "sense_id": "ef594758-21a0-3a71-b6f2-94591afa7244",
                    "sense_definition": "A measure of relativistic velocity, mathematically defined as the hyperbolic arctangent of the speed relative to the speed of light.",
                    "learner_level": "C2",
                    "frequency": "VeryLow",
                    "semantic_group_id": "physics_measure",
                    "name_type": "no",
                    "examples": [
                        {
                            "text": "In special relativity, <w>rapidity</w> is advantageous because it is additive under collinear boosts."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Physicists calculated the <w>rapidity</w> of the accelerated particles before colliding them in the chamber."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "sense_id": "6c07e253-6d2b-3ed4-a11a-ae6b1e02a5a8",
                    "sense_definition": "A measure of the velocity of a subatomic particle in a beam relative to the beam's axis.",
